      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8a304e7d",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the thief in the act of theft",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (person) stealing the bicycle, as the meme's humor and message are directed at the viewer by implying they are the one in the situation (the thief). The text 'pedal faster patrick' uses a generic placeholder name, but the context of the scene and the imperative tone of the text ('pedal faster') creates an implicit 'you' projection, making the viewer feel personally implicated in the scenario of being caught stealing.",
